-- title:
--   Newform part of parabolic cohomology over any algebraically closed field
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$, a finite set $S$ of natural numbers all of which are prime and which contains every prime factor of $N$, and an algebraically closed field $F$ of characteristic zero. Fix $M_g\ge 1$ with $M_g\mid N$, a weight-two cusp form $g$ on $\Gamma_0(M_g)$ satisfying [`CuspForm.IsNewform`](def/CuspForm_Newforms.html#L23) (its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices and the two prime-power recursions, and no divisor $M\mid N$, $M\neq N$ carries a normalised eigenform with the same $a_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$), and a ring homomorphism $\chi_g$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra Mg 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(M_g)))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M_g$ and the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid M_g$ — to $\mathbb{C}$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ and $\chi_g(U_q)=a_q(g)$. Fix a ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the image of $\chi_g$ to $F$ and an arbitrary family $(\lambda_q)_{q\in\mathbb N}$ in $F$. Work on $H^1(N,\top;F)$ with the transfer operators [`CohCarrier.heckeTL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23), $\varphi\mapsto \mathrm{cores}(\varphi\circ \mathrm{conjL}_\ell)$, and the submodule of parabolic homomorphisms, those additive maps $\mathrm{Additive}\,\Gamma_0(N)\to F$ vanishing on all $\gamma$ with $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2=4$. Two assertions are made. First, for every prime $\ell\notin S$ and every $\mu\in F$, a parabolic class lying in the maximal generalised $\mu$-eigenspace of the $\ell$-th operator lies in its $\mu$-eigenspace. Second, the $F$-dimension of the intersection of the parabolic submodule with $\bigcap_{\ell \text{ prime},\,\ell\notin S}\ker\bigl(T_\ell-\iota\chi_g(T_\ell)\bigr)$ and with $\bigcap_{q \text{ prime},\,q\mid N}$ the maximal generalised $\lambda_q$-eigenspace of the $q$-th operator equals $2\prod_{q\mid N}\mathrm{mult}_{\lambda_q}(P_q)$, the product over the prime factors of $N$, where, with $a_q=\iota\chi_g(U_q)$ if $q\mid M_g$ and $a_q=\iota\chi_g(T_q)$ otherwise and $e=v_q(N)-v_q(M_g)$, one has $P_q=X-a_q$ when $e=0$ and $P_q=X^{e-1}\bigl(X^2-a_qX+c_q\bigr)$ otherwise, with $c_q=0$ for $q\mid M_g$ and $c_q=q$ for $q\nmid M_g$ (and $P_q=1$ for non-prime $q$).
--
--   This is the Atkin–Lehner–Li count of the $g$-isotypic part of parabolic cohomology in weight two, in the form needed over an arbitrary algebraically closed field of characteristic zero: the local factor at $q\mid N$ is the characteristic polynomial of $U_q$ on the oldform string of $g$ of length $v_q(N)-v_q(M_g)+1$. It is obtained from the corresponding statement over $\mathbb{C}$ by base change along an integral basis of parabolic classes, and it feeds the computation of corner submodules and the construction of algebra homomorphisms out of local Hecke algebras.
